WEBVTT

NOTE
map-my-folder-process — 18 cues. Every cue is the on-screen headline of its beat,
verbatim. No cue introduces text that is not on screen in that beat. Beat 00 (cover)
and beat 19 (close) carry no cue by decision; the stop's tail after cue 18 is silent
by decision. Timings are the film's own frame table plus the measured read length.

1
00:00:01.933 --> 00:00:03.423
Nothing is opened yet.

2
00:00:06.533 --> 00:00:09.223
Sixty-two files, and the shape is already visible.

3
00:00:11.933 --> 00:00:13.653
Four folders. One shape.

4
00:00:15.933 --> 00:00:18.073
And one file the blueprint does not have.

5
00:00:19.933 --> 00:00:21.933
Seven types. A closed set.

6
00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:27.023
Run them in order. First pass wins.

7
00:00:29.933 --> 00:00:33.003
Copy or reference? They look identical from outside.

8
00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:38.123
Nineteen exact lines — including the template's own instructions.

9
00:00:40.333 --> 00:00:42.843
One line, telling the next contributor to add a file.

10
00:00:44.933 --> 00:00:47.813
Four READMEs exist. All of them one level deeper.

11
00:00:50.333 --> 00:00:53.163
Five words in this repo carry two meanings each.

12
00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:56.423
region is the one that costs the most.

13
00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:00.793
Each card is shorter than the file it points at.

14
00:01:03.933 --> 00:01:05.933
Seven cards over sixty-two files.

15
00:01:08.933 --> 00:01:10.003
Ask it something.

16
00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:15.053
Catalog row, then one card.

17
00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:20.783
Three transcripts. The honest comparison is narrow.

18
00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:24.713
One file opened, then stop.
